    },
    {
      "text": "Details and Ablation on Sampling Strategies",
      "bbox": [
        132.07960510253906,
        528.8037719726562,
        320.0040588378906,
        537.7601318359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this section, we first introduce the different sampling strategies supported by LLaDA. We then",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        549.559326171875,
        503.99749755859375,
        558.4658813476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "present ablation studies to evaluate the performance of these sampling strategies.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        560.4683837890625,
        429.6923828125,
        569.3749389648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Flexible Sampling Strategies. In Sec. 2.4, Fig. 2 (c) illustrates the reverse generation process of",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        576.7367553710938,
        503.99761962890625,
        585.7628784179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaDA. As shown in Fig. 4, in addition to the reverse generation process, LLaDA also supports",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        587.766357421875,
        503.9974060058594,
        596.6729125976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "autoregressive and block diffusion [31] sampling directly after the pre-training or SFT stages, without",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        598.6753540039062,
        503.9979553222656,
        607.5819091796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "requiring any further modifications or retraining. Block diffusion sampling applies the origin reverse",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        609.5843505859375,
        503.998046875,
        618.4909057617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "process within each block and the autoregressive sampling across blocks. In the original block",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        620.4933471679688,
        504.2514953613281,
        629.39990234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diffusion process, the sequence length varies dynamically. As shown in Fig. 4 (c), LLaDA can also",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        631.40234375,
        503.9965515136719,
        640.3088989257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "adopt a fixed-length block diffusion strategy, which we refer to as block diffusion LLaDA, also known",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        642.3113403320312,
        504.0013732910156,
        651.2178955078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "as semi-autoregressive remasking.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        653.2203369140625,
        244.40792846679688,
        662.1268920898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Experimental Setup. We evaluate different sampling strategies using both LLaDA 8B Base and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        669.4898071289062,
        503.99725341796875,
        678.5159301757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LLaDA 8B Instruct for comprehensive analysis. For LLaDA 8B Base, we use the five benchmarks in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        680.5183715820312,
        504.00048828125,
        689.4249267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tab. 1 that are evaluated based on sampling rather than likelihood estimation. For LLaDA 8B Instruct,",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        691.4273681640625,
        505.2447509765625,
        700.3339233398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we use the seven metrics in Tab. 2, excluding MMLU and HellaSwag, since these two tasks only",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        702.3363647460938,
        504.3495178222656,
        711.242919921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "require the model to generate a single token (i.e., A, B, C, or D). In all settings, one token is generated",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        713.245361328125,
        504.00140380859375,
        722.1519165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
